  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Attack and defence 2v2",
  "description": "Four lines, one in each corner. The two lines by one goal are defenders (A and B), the two by the other goal are attackers (C and D). A starts the drill with a long diagonal pass to D. C and D attack together, passing back and forth and using passes and fakes to get past the defenders to a shot. A and B step out and defend in front of the goalkeeper but may not cross the centre line.\n\nSwap roles between the lines after a while. Go back along the long sides, outside the cones, so no one collides. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Attack: pass along the floor and show with your stick where you want the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Attack: run at a defender to commit them, then pass."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Defence: talk to each other – who takes the ball carrier?"
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
